# Files NOT to upload when deploying with the Vercel CLI.
#
# NOTE: when a .vercelignore exists, Vercel uses IT (not .gitignore) to decide
# what to upload. We deliberately do NOT list js/config.js here, so the CLI
# (`vercel --prod`) uploads your local token file and the deployed site works.
# Your token still stays OUT of GitHub because .gitignore still excludes it.
#
# ⚠️ A static site's JS is public, so anyone who opens the deployed URL can read
# the token in the page source. Only deploy a SHORT-LIVED hackathon token and
# regenerate it after the event. For production, use a serverless proxy instead.

.git
node_modules
*.log
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode
.idea
